      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-03_WidnesExaminer_art0007" n="art0007">
        <head>WIDNES AND WARRINGTON.</head>
        <p>WIDNES AND WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>MR. JOHN E. GOODWIN continues to make ADVANCE S FRIVATELY to Tradesmen, Farmers. Working-men, and all respectable Hcuseholders, on their own security. 010NEY TO INCREASE YOUR STOCK. MONEY TO FURNISH YOUR HOUSE.</p>
        <p>MONEY TO PAY RENT OR DEBTS. Without Bondsmen, without delay, without public enquiry, on your simple written prcrnise to pay back.—Apply r t VIC- TORIA CHAMBERS (foot of the Central Station), WIDNES, and in WARRINGTON at my Residence, 134, Orford-lane, any Evening. Applications from RUNCORN *rid DiEstriot, generally receive precisely the same attention.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-03_WidnesExaminer_art0008" n="art0008">
        <head>MONEY. MONEY. MONEY.</head>
        <p>MONEY. MONEY. MONEY.</p>
        <p>APRIVATE GENTLEMAN with a big capital at his disposal is open to advance Loans daily from £2 upwards. No fees charged. Nosecurity required. Simply en note of hand. Distance no object.—Apply personally or by letter to MANAGER, 6, Cross Lane, Earlestown (private house). flours 9 a.m. to 8 p.m. Strictest privacy guaran- ecd. Special terms to Farmers.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-03_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <head>AUTUMN AND WINTER FASHIONS</head>
        <p>AUTUMN AND WINTER FASHIONS</p>
        <p>W. HODGKINSON, LIMITED, 46 &amp; 48, BRIDGE-STREET, WARRINGTON. SPECIAL SII OW</p>
        <p>OF THE NEWEST FASHIONS ON NEXT TUESDAY, WEDNESDAY,</p>
        <p>SEPTEMBER 29TH &amp; 30TH,</p>
        <p>AND FOLLOWING DAYS.</p>
        <p>The Various</p>
        <p>SHOW ROOMS</p>
        <p>Are replete with N OVELTIES IN MANTLES, COSTUMES MILLINERY, AND OUTFITTING.</p>
        <p>MAGNIFICENT SILKS FOR GOWNS AND BLOUSES. EXCLUSIVE DESIGNS IN ROBES AND DRESS MATERIALS. LADIES' TEA GOWNS, DRESSING GOWNS</p>
        <p>AND BEAUTIFUL UNDERWEAR.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-03_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <p>DUNVILLR'S OLD IRISH WHISKY</p>
        <p>Has gained SEVENTEEN MEDALS at various great Inter- national Exhibitions. _ _</p>
        <p>It is sold by every respectable dealer in the world. Quota- tions „on application to the Head 0 faces, Belfast. x</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1896-10-03_WidnesExaminer_art0011" n="art0011">
        <p>FOR THE NEXT MONTH OUR ANNUAL STOCK- TAKING S aLE TAKES PLACE, IN ORDER TO CLEAR OUR LARGE AND VARIED STOCK OF jN'EW AND 13 CO ND-H AND GOODS WE HAVE RE-MARKED THE WHOLE STOCK AT PRICES THAT MUST ASTOUND ALL. LOW PRICES AND GOOD QUALITY IS OUR MOTTO. IF YOU DO NOT WANT FURNITURE JUST AT PRESENT WE WILL KEEP IT ANY REASONABLE TIME ON PAY- MENT OF A SMALL DEP.:SIT, AND MAKE NO CHARGE FOR STORAGE OR DELIVERY. NOW IS YOUR TIME TO SECURE CREAT BARGAINS. OUR MAMMOTH ESTABLISHMENT IS BRIM-FULL WITH BARGAINS ALL MARKED IN PLAIN FIGURES FROM WHICH WE DEDUCT 5 PER CENT DURING THE SALE ONLY. GREAT STOCKTAKING SALE. WE INTEND DURING THE NEXT MONTH TO PUL- VERISE THE FURNISHING TRADE IN THE NORTH OF ENGLAND, AND THE PRICES WE ARE OFFERING GOODS AT IS ENOUGH TO MAKE ALL THE OTHER FURNISHING HOUSES CLOSE AT ONCE. WE MUST AND WILL CLEAR OUT OUR STOCK IN THE NEXT FOUR WEEKS AT GIVING-AWAY PRICES. REMEMBER, WE HAVE ONLY ONE SALE A YEAR, AND WE KEEP STORING ALL THE GREAT BAR- GAINS WHICH WE COLLECT FOR THIS ANNUAL SALE NOW ON. GREAT STOCKTAKING SALE. WE EXPECT SUCH A RUSH THAT WE HAVE TO ASK THE INDULGENCE OF CUSTOMERS TO GIVE US AS ' MUCH TIME AS POSSIBLE TO DELIVER THEIR PUR- CHASES, OUR PACKINa AND POLISHING DEPART- MENTS ARE LARGELY AUGMENTED, AND STILL WORKING TILL 10 OR 11 O'CLOCK EACH EVENING, SO AS TO GET THE GOODS AWAY AS QUICKLY AS POS- SIBLE. PURCHASERS WILL DO WELL TO CALL EARLY AND SECURE THE BARGAINS. IF YOU LEAVE IT TOO LONG THEY WILL BE GONE, AND YOU WILL BE DIS- APPOINTED, WE GIVE BELOW A FEW PARTICULARS OF BAR- GAINS NOW ON VIEW, SPACE PaEVENIING US FROM GIVING A LARGER LIST. LOT 1.-Very Handsome Chippendale DRAWING-ROOM St IT E in very expensive Silk Tapestry, expen- sively carved frames, second-hand, just been re-upholstered and re-polished ; our pr'ce £l2 12a ; cost. £25. LOT 2.-Strong and Serviceable LEATHER SUITE, with large-sized Couch and Easy Chair, also four small Chairs, hardly soiled, for £3 19s 6cl • worth £lO. LOT 3.-Very Massive Pollard Oak DINING-R, IOM SUITE in Lister's best Velvee, second-hand, but as good as new ; Couch, pair of luxurious Easy Chairs, and six padded Spoon-back Chairs, artistically carved tops; well worth £5O; our price £25. LOT 4.-The Very Handsome SIDEBOARD in rich English Oak, 6ft long, and nearly lift high, with lofty bevel-plate back, and the usual conveniences in bottom part, equal to new in every respect. ju,t been scraped and re-polished ; cheap at £45. We are delivering it free for 22 guineas. LOT 5.-Beautiful SUITE in Levant Leather, suitable for parlour or dining-room, nicely upholstered and deeply tufted, in solid frames., as good as new, for £6 lbs; worth £l5. LOT 6.- Very nice Walnut CABINET, nearly 4ft wide, with lofty glass back, all bevel plates, with shelves and cupboards ; cost £lO ; our price £3 33. Just been re-polished. LOT 7.-Solid Walnut DRAWING-ROOM SUITE in expen- sive Brocade Velvet, Small Chairs handsomely carved ; a bargain, for £lO 10s. LOT 8.-Solid Walnut SUITE in Velvet, not quite so good as the above Let, to be sold for £8 153 ; worth double. LoT 9.-Massive DINING-TABLE, opens to sft., suitable for 12 persons so dine, polished walnut colorer; a bargain. for £2ss. LOT 10.-Very noble-looking SIDEBOARD, solid walnut sft. long, with lofty glass back, drawers, cupboards, shelves, &amp;c. ; second-hand and better thannew, for £8 15s. ; worth £2O. CATALOGUES CAN BE HAD POST FREE OR ON APPLICATION. . LOT 11.-Capital 4ft. Mahogany SIDEBOARD, with bevelled plate-glass back, thoroughly well made ; worth £lO ; only asking £slss. LOT 12.-The Handsomest DRAWING-ROOM SUITE in Manchester, upholstered with very expensive and choice colour Genoa Velvet, and Solid Rosewood frames, beautifully inlaid with real ivory. The Couch Is very pretty, each end different design ; pair of comfortable Easy Chairs, four Smalls, and two nicely made Occasional. ; just been re-upholstered and re•polished, anal in condition equal to new ; only ask- ing 29 guineas ; well worth £5O LOTS 13r0 2E-Twelve Walnut Maliegany and Rosewood OVERMANTELS, in all sizes and prices, from 12a 6d to £2 10s. Loa's 25 TO 47.-Twenty-three Walnut Mahogany and Chip- pendale OVERMANTLES, in all Biz-. 3 and shapes, from £2 128 6d, to £l2. LOT 48.-Large-size Gilt CHIMNEY GLASS, real British plate and English Gold, goad as new, £1 17e 6d ; cost £3 10s. LOT 0.-Four sets of FIRE SETS in solid brass.comprising massive Curb, set of beautiful Fire Brasses and one pair Rests, all complete for 21s ; worth £2 ss. LoT 50.-Grand Dining-room Black and Copper CURB SET, Including Brasses, Stop and Dogs in grand condition cost £lO, our price for sale £3 15s ; a bargain. Lox 51.-Fine Baltic Oak BINING-RtiOd SUITE in green Morocco, second-hann in condition as good as new; thefull nine pieces tor £l3 13s ; worth £2O. LOT 52.-Very Fancy DRAWING-ROOM SUITE in green stamped Velvet beantitullv upholstered all small chairs padded backs; a bargain for £i 15s. LOT 53.-Well-made BOOKCASE and CHEFFONIER in Solid Mahogany.nearly 4ft wide with two glass doors in too part ; second-hand but as good as new ; just been re-polished : only £4 lbs ; worth £lO. LOT 54.-Very Fine Chippendale Mahogany BOOKCASE and CHEFFONIER. by Maple, richly-carved panels, and fitted with movable shelves and brackets ; thoroughly overhauled ; cost £25; our price £l2 10s. IF WE DO NOT ADVERTISE THE ARTICLE YOU ARE IN NEED OF, JUST GIVE US A CALL. WE CAN FIND YOU A BARGAIN IN THE GOODS YOU. WAN LOT 55.-Handsome pair of Polished Walnut TOILET TABLES, bevelled plates to both stands, complete with drawers and shelves ; worth £0; only ask £3 15s. ; just been re-polished. LOT 56.-Solid Cyprus Satin Walnut Pair of Enclosed DRESSING-TABLE AND WASHSTAND, fitted with bevelled pl ttes, marble alab, and tile back; extraordinary value ; £615,., with towel rail ; worth double. LOT 57.-The Cheapest and Best Second-hand BEDROOM SUITE in Manchester. Solid Satin Walnut Ward- robe, pair of solid Stands,Towel Rail, and two Chairs; marvellous value ; £23 lbs. LoT $B.-Large BEDROOM SUITE, all solid polished walnut second-hand ; price £l2 125,; Neat f2O. LOT 59.-Massiva 7tt. Solid America Walnut BEDROOM SUITE, lately removed from Alderley ; sft. Chnval Dressing Table and 4ft. Gin. Washstand (the carving and bevelled plates are superb) 3 velvet-seated Chairs, Towel Airer and Bedside Pedestal well worth £l5O. Delivered free for 65 guineas. LOT 60.-Very fine sft. &amp;tin aN smut and Ash BEDROOM SUITE. with large-size Toilet Table and the full complement of articles, as good as new; lately cost £65 ; our price £27 10s. A decided bargain. LOT 61 ._Elegant 7ft BEDROOM SUITE in solid walnut, the Wardrobe fitted with bow front and large hanging compartments each side, with large bevelled silvered plates in front, interior fitted with drawers, cup- boards, hangers, and bonnet-boxes. A grand article. The 4lt Gin Wash-board and Dressing-Table is in unison with the Wardrobe, and is a masterpiece of cabinet-making. The price we want for his Suite is not £2OO, but 75 guineas-not the price of the tables. LoT 62.-Very nice polished Walnut BEDROOM SUITE. comprising large-size Robe, with bevelled plate centre door, pair of large Toilet Tables, fitted with drawers to both, marble slab and tile back ; Towel Rail, and three Cane Chairs ; second-11,nd, just been re-pol- ished ; once £8 17s 6d ; well worth £2O Lore 63 to 69.- Six pairs of Enamelled WASHSTAND and DRESSING-TABLES, from 12s. 6d. to 22s 6d; all worth double. LOT 70.-Six Doz. CANE CHAIRS at 2. 3d each for not less than three.</p>
        <p>FULL PARTICULARS OF THE ABOVE LOTS BY POST OR ON APPLICATION. LOT 71.—Six full-size Black and Brass FRENCH BED- STEADS, very heavy and well finished. for 141 6d ; worth 21. LOT 72.-12' Good WOOL BEDS. full size and well nee, with two Pillows and Bolster oomplete ; 14. 6d each to clear. LOT 73.-50 Pairs of full-size STitAW PALLIASSES at ss; ordinary mice 8s 6d. LOT 74.- 30 WOVEN WIRE MATTRESSES, fit any full sized bedstead, pitchpine frames; 9s. lid.; worth 18s 6d. LOT 75.—Three FEATHER BEDS complete, thoroughly purified, 501 b weight, in good linen tick, for 35s ; ordinare poice, 50s. LOT 76.—Grand Brass ITALIAN BEDSTEAD, all solid, with patent wire mattresses attached; a bargain for 455. LOT 77.-12 Splendid WOOL MATTRESSES, very heavy and good, full size; 14s 6d cacti to clear. Lo T 78,—Three INSTITUTION BEDSTEADS, very heavy, with Double Woven Wire Mattresses attached; sale prise. 21s. Lois 75.—Grand HOUSS OF FURNITURE; usual price £l5; sale prices £l2 ; complete with all the requisites for a small cottage. Delivered free. Lox 80.—Our £2O HOUSE OF FURNITURE cannot be beaten by any other h Ala. under £3O; contains Fur- niture for Two Bedrooms, Parlour and Kitchen ; sec, nd-hand, but nearly new. A bargain. LOTS 81 To 87. Seven complete HOUSES OF FURNITURE, ranging from £25 tck £150; suitable for houses at a rental from les. weekly to £5O yearly. Grand value dining the Sale.</p>
        <p>REMEMBER OUR GREAT STOCKTAKING SALO. THE GREAT EVENT OF THE YEAR. GOLDSTONE AND SONS THE GREAT HOUSE FURNISHERS , 115, 117, 119, OXFORD-STREET (Opposite AlfS^lnts' Church, MANCHESTRE. •</p>
      </div>
