        <head>MINEH.</head>
        <p>MINEH.</p>
        <p>ER 3rd, 1896.</p>
        <p>I no subject which eI" 1 public attention in as that relating to it is true, been a con- agitation during the ie to any lessening of to the fact that mos' re organised to give the country have aoW we certainly answered promotersjr had our own Government that the people of 00 imous in their desire or all to Turkish ems to have had aT3' mivincing COAtinental thing" policy which weeks is a failure. ing the SULTAN a free ristian subjects in or- ing "of the dreaded w recognised that if massacre the EasterO n spite of all preceir s which have occurred licate in which dire' g. In the first place Ling in the attitude a mtinental Powers to' irse of a special inter Ambassador, lt I decidedly menaciog entate. The SULTO toned with seriongi iot show a decide('</p>
