        <p>and Mrs W S Graves, Venetian glass bowl ; Sir Charles E Hamilton, Bart. pair Sevre3 lases Mr A B Batchelor, silver snuff box ; Mrs Clelland, silver salver; Rev J J Sandys, silver-gilt inkstand; Mr D G Irvine, silver snuff box; Mr. and Mrs Bradstock Lockett, pair fruit dishes and spoons; Mr and Mrs J Monro. silver object glass; Mrs Godfrey Armytage, silver punch ladle; Lord and Lady Skelmersdale, Sheffield plate; Mr. and Hon. Mrs Oke.over. silver-mounted Norwegian tankard; Mr L S Cohen. pair of bronze figures; Mr G II Robertson, silver vase ; Mr T B Mor- gan. Nuremberg cup; Gateacre inhabitants, gilt cbck and vases; Mess! s Rimmer. rosewood cabinet; Mr T Jones, silver match box ; Viscount Valletort, bamboo stick; tradesmen of Liverpool silver tea service (for bride); ditto, silver punch bowl ; Mr and Mrs F R Hughes, Venetian glass; Gateacre servants and employees. silysr-glit dessert spoons ; Mr and Mrs Christie. ivory panels ; Mr Leyland, naturalist, book; Mr GI H Thompson, silver cigarette case; Messrs S and J Dennis, silver castor and spoons ; Mr Leonard Pilkington,gold lacquer tray; Countess of Ayiesford, sugar sifter ; Mr. and Mrs Edward Hacking, silver almond dishes; Mr and Mrs C Mason, ivory figures; Mr and Mrs Chapple Gill, silver bowl ; Mr Dudley Forwood, silver Nuremberg cups ; Mr R F Gladstone; silver peoper mills; Mr and Mrs Molyneux Seel, silver setling-wax case; Mr C H Brancker, old slyer box Mr and Mrs William Turner,Over. pearl pin; Mr and Mrs Henry Greenall, silver jug ; Mr and Mrs Willis, silver and platinum teacup; Earl of Derby. old silvar dessert dishes George 11. ; Leicester employees, hunting crop; Mrs Bagot, blackthorn hunting crop; Mr and Mrs Henry Tate,jun., silver inkstand; Mr Earnest Pilkington, silver mounted quaich ; Dr Henry Gorst. gold jewelled cup; Mr E S Gladstone. engraving; Mr and Mrs Stanley Owen. silver beaker ; Mr and Mrs Harry Tinsley, silver box ; Colonel and Mrs Clifton Brown, silver bowl ; Mr and Mrs H C Neilson. Dresden vases; Miss Sh-zidan, diamond pin, gold cigarette case, and gold mounted pocket book ; Mr H 13 Lambe, model; Mr and Mrs J If Stock, hot water can, silver-mounted; Mr and Mrs H Lyster, silver canoe cigarette case ; Sir Arthur and Lady Forwood, silver porringer salver; Mr and Mrs Hugh Melly, Dutch silver chairs and table ; Mr and Mrs H A Graves, coal- port, vase; Mr and Mrs Leo Pilkington, china figures ; Mrs John Wrigley, screen, hand-painted by self ; Mr. and Mrs J G Livingston, picture (water-colour) ; Mr H K Aspinall, ser- viette rings ; Mr A Eccles. engraving,Landseer ; employees of P Walker and Son, Warrington and Burton, Limited, silver statue self and The Soarer; employees of P Walker and Son, W and B. Limited, hunting saddle and bridle, with acces- sories in silver, gold-mounted hunting orop (for bride); Mr N Darbyshire, gold cigarette holder ; Major Drury. Indian vases. Mr Snewing, driving whip; Captain L H Jones. silver match-box; servants, Sandy Brow, hunting crop ;Mr and Mrs Bullock. silv,r inkstand; Mr J Fulton Smith, shyer cigar case ;Mr B W Edmondson, port and starboard lights ; Mr and Mrs G A Lockett. crown Derby vase ; Captain and Mrs W H Edwardes, ivory paper knife; Mr W S Higgin, sil- ver cigarette box.</p>
